{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1482280-interesting-new-gods","id":1482280,"title":"Interesting New Gods","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scion"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-05-29T12:29:31-07:00","id":1482280,"title":"Interesting New Gods","content":"So I'm running a Scion game and one of my players discovered Malinalxochitl, Mexihcah goddess of desert animals and witchcraft and (from what I could find online) an antagonistic figure in the founding myth of Tenochtitlan. Which we immediately put together a list of purviews and callings for for her. So that got me thinking. Has anyone else had a player (or as a GM themself) found any interesting deities that you put rules down for? If so, which ones?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12743-kamenhero25","name":"kamenhero25","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12743_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-29T15:23:43-07:00","id":1482294,"title":"","content":"I wrote something for Phanes, an independent deity, associated with Ancient Iran. He/she/they were associated with time, creation, justice, and fate. But I misplaced it long ago. I'd need better research facilities than I have now to reconstruct what I wrote.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-30T07:33:03-07:00","id":1482372,"title":"","content":"I can't recall her name ATM but there is supposed to be a Loa of the marketplace and trade IIRC.<br /> <br /> update: Ayizan is her name.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":12890,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","user":"No One of Consequence","date":". 06-01-2022, 04:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-02T11:38:14-07:00","id":1482804,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>kamenhero25</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1482280-interesting-new-gods#post1482280\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So I'm running a Scion game and one of my players discovered Malinalxochitl, Mexihcah goddess of desert animals and witchcraft and (from what I could find online) an antagonistic figure in the founding myth of Tenochtitlan. Which we immediately put together a list of purviews and callings for for her. So that got me thinking. Has anyone else had a player (or as a GM themself) found any interesting deities that you put rules down for? If so, which ones?</div> </div> </div> </div>I found an entire site with Sumerians Gods, the Annunaki, and an entire new &quot;Titan&quot; who is friendly... In their meta, the Annunaki had left to live inside the Great Titan, the primordial Stars of the Sky. It's pretty awesome. It also had many new powers, like an entire purview just for &quot;inventions&quot;, for Gods like Hephaestus and such","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24689-kakost","name":"Kakost","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-02T12:39:17-07:00","id":1482813,"title":"","content":"The Annuna are in <b>Scion: Demigod</b>, along with the Apu (Incan), the Atua (Polynesian), the Tengri (Mongolian), and the Bogovi (Slavs). <b>Mysteries of the World</b> gives us the Loa (Haiti), the Nemetondavos (Gaul), and the Yazata (Persia). <b>Scion: God</b> will be introducing a few more, though I'm not recalling which ones at the moment. <br /> <br /> In terms of individual gods of existing Pantheons, my personal favorite is Iris of the Theoi, goddess of the rainbow and a messenger of the gods, like Hermes. I prefer to give her something of a modern update where she's expanded \u201cthe rainbow\u201d to \u201cthe electromagnetic spectrum\u201d: ultraviolet, X-rays, gamma rays, infrared, microwaves, and radio waves, as well as ROYGBIV.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-03T00:50:41-07:00","id":1482904,"title":"","content":"Our storyteller introduced <span style=\"color:#202122\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Huehuec\u00f3yotl of the Teotle as mantle of coyote. He was the father of the our Hero main villain.</span></span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/490-omenseer","name":"omenseer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar490_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"987"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-23T08:34:51-07:00","id":1484777,"title":"","content":"Having now obtained my copy of Demigod and confirmed that he isn't in it, I've been obliged to make my own version of the Hawaiian shark god Kamohoali'i.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12108-gscrap","name":"gscra